<title>BRAZIL: Bahia cocoa arrivals 2.90 mln bags by May 4.</title>
<headline>Bahia cocoa arrivals 2.90 mln bags by May 4.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bahia 1996/97 cocoa arrivals totaled 2,896,069 million 60-kg bags by the week ending May 4 compared with 2,673,171 bags by May 5, 1996, traders said.</p>
<p>This marked the end of the 1996/97 crop, they added.</p>
<p>Arrivals in the four weeks from April 7 to May 4 were as follows in 60-kg bags according to figures from the Brazilian Cocoa Trade Commission Comcauba, traders said.</p>
<p> WEEK		   1996/97   1995/96   Accumulated 1996/97</p>
<p> April 7-13	   15,798    13,504	 2,850,499</p>
<p> April 14-20	  12,576     9,229	 2,863,075</p>
<p> April 21-27	  15,839     7,164	 2,878,914</p>
<p> April 28-May 4     17,155    16,606	 2,896,069</p>
<p>No figures are so far available for the 1997/98 midcrop which traditionally begins in May but which has been delayed this year due to dry weather earlier in the season. ((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
